course: dictionary
lesson: 15654
title: Formal words: therein
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like a letter from a bank or a page from an old book. Therein is one of them. You can work out its meaning from its parts: there and in. Therein means "in that place, thing or document". «The box was empty, but the note inside was long, and therein I found a clue.» Here, therein means "in that note".
explain: Check a meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. «The rules are printed on the back of the ticket, so read therein.» Swap therein for "in it" and you get "read in it", which still makes sense. So therein means "in that", and you have found its meaning.
explain: Therein also appears in the phrase therein lies. It means "that is where something is found". «The sea was rough and the boat was small. Therein lies the danger.» The danger is found in the rough sea and the small boat. Read the words around it, and the meaning becomes clear.
fact: Therein is a formal adverb. It means in that place, thing or document.
fact: Therein is made of "there" and "in", so it means "in that".
fact: «Therein lies» means that is where something is found, as in «Therein lies the problem».
fact: You will find therein in legal papers, old books and some everyday writing.
exercise: «The old map showed a cave, and therein was a hidden treasure chest.» What does therein mean here? | On the top of the hill | *In that cave | Far away over the sea | Under a big tree
exercise: «Therein lies the problem.» What does this phrase mean? | The problem is very big and scary | The problem has gone away | *That is where the problem is found | Nobody knows about the problem
exercise: «The letter was short, but therein was the news we had waited for.» Find and copy the word that means "in that letter". | *therein | short | letter | waited
test: «The forest was dark and quiet, and therein lived many owls.» What does therein mean? | *In that forest | Far away from home | At the bottom of the lake | Under the bed
test: Ella says therein is just a fancy word for there. Is she right? | No, it means away from home | *Not quite, but it is close, and it means in that place or thing like "in it" | Yes, it means exactly the same as there | No, it means in that place or thing, like "in it"
exam: «The notebook was locked, and therein were all our secret plans.» What does therein tell you? | *The plans were kept inside the notebook | The plans were written on the wall | The plans were lost in the rain | The notebook was sold at the market
